From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 13:02:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 371/638] cef: guard DevTools opener propagation

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: clean-chrome-cef-devtools-boundary
ROOT_CAUSE: The CEF DevTools patch assigned Browser::CreateParams::opener in enable_cef=false builds even though that member is intentionally CEF-only.
FIX_REASON: Keep opener propagation inside the same ENABLE_CEF buildflag boundary as the field and delegate path.
SCOPE: chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
VALIDATION: The previously failing AROS devtools_window.o rebuilt successfully in the full Chrome tree.
RISK: Additional incomplete CEF integration guards may surface as the clean Chrome build continues.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: full Chrome compile -> missing opener member -> inspect CEF patch and Browser definition -> align assignment guard -> focused object PASS.
Evidence:-chromium-browser-renderer-20260728/build-09-full-resume.log;-chromium-browser-renderer-20260728/build-10-devtools-cef-opener.log
Job:
---
 chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc b/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
index d102fff3e9..df3811517f 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/devtools/devtools_window.cc
@@ -1868,7 +1868,9 @@ void DevToolsWindow::CreateDevToolsBrowser() {
 
   if (!browser_) {
     auto create_params = Browser::CreateParams::CreateForDevTools(profile_);
+#if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_CEF)
     create_params.opener = opener;
+#endif
 
     browser_ = Browser::Create(std::move(create_params));
     browser_->tab_strip_model()->AddWebContents(
